@*
    ── משאבים (Lecturer) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
    Visual source:  design/design-system/MotivaLecturerDesign/
                    Motiva Lecturer Resources.dc.html
                    משאבים מרצה 268.pdf

    The screen itself now lives in ResourcesLibrary, which the mentor renders
    too — same title row, same stage strip, same chips, same card grid, same
    detail panel. This page contributes only what is LECTURER-specific:

      • the route and its [Authorize(Admin, Staff)] gate;
      • GetAllAsync — api/resourcefiles, the Admin/Staff endpoint, so the
        lecturer sees every resource in the system rather than a scoped feed;
      • CanManage — the "ניהול משאבים" link into /management/resources and the
        empty-state CTA beside it. Upload / edit / delete still live there,
        unchanged;
      • the stage resolver — api/dashboard at lecturer scope, which only
        Admin/Staff may request;
      • the lecturer's own favourites key.

    Nothing about the approved layout moved or changed in the extraction.
*@

@page "/resource-files"
@layout AppLayout
@attribute [Authorize(Roles = Roles.Admin + "," + Roles.Staff)]
@namespace AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.ResourceFiles
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authorization
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Pages.Learning
@using AuthWithAdmin.Client.Services

@inject IResourceFilesService     ResourceFilesService
@inject IDashboardOverviewService DashboardService

<ResourcesLibrary Title="משאבים"
                  Subtitle="נהלים, מחוונים וחומרי הוראה — לכל הקורס"
                  Loader="ResourceFilesService.GetAllAsync"
                  FavoritesKey="motiva.lecturer.resources.favorites"
                  CurrentStageLoader='@ResourceStageSources.FromDashboardOverview(DashboardService, "lecturer")'
                  CanManage="true" />
